#: ../../solid/index.rst:2
msgid "固体物理"
msgstr "Solid-State Physics"

#: ../../solid/index.rst:4
msgid ""
"結晶構造と\\ :ref:`逆格子<reciprocal-"
"lattice>`、結晶の対称性、単位胞の取り直しを出発点に、周期系の電子状態、エネルギーバンド、k点積分へ進みます。続いて、原子の振動を\\ :ref:`フォノン<phonon>`\\ "
"として扱い、振動の不安定性から構造の変化を考えます。最後に、格子の変形や対称性が電子状態や\\ :ref:`分極<spontaneous-polarization>`\\ "
"にどう関わるかを見ます。"
msgstr ""
"We start with crystal structure and the \\ :ref:`reciprocal lattice <reciprocal-lattice>`, "
"crystal symmetry, and the choice of unit cell. We then turn to electronic states in periodic "
"systems, energy bands, and k-point integration. We describe atomic vibrations in terms of \\ "
":ref:`phonons <phonon>`\\  and examine how vibrational instabilities can change the structure. "
"Finally, we look at how lattice deformation and symmetry affect electronic states and \\ "
":ref:`polarization <spontaneous-polarization>`\\ ."

